flowchart TB
  accTitle: Lazygit Panels and Common Shortcuts
  accDescr: Lazygit presents files, branches, commits, stashes, and diffs in one interface. Stage and inspect changes from Files, manage history through Branches and Commits, and store temporary work with Stash. Global keys control focus, movement, undo, refresh, and exit.
  subgraph working["Inspect working tree changes"]
    direction LR
    files["Files<br/>Space to stage · a to stage all<br/>c to commit · Shift+A to amend"]
    diff["Diff preview<br/>Inspect added and removed lines<br/>Use Space to stage a hunk in the diff"]
    files -->|"Enter to view diff"| diff
  end
  subgraph history["Manage repository history"]
    direction LR
    branches["Branches<br/>Space to switch · n to create<br/>M to merge · r to rebase"]
    commits["Commits<br/>Enter to inspect · i to rebase<br/>c to copy commits · v to paste"]
    stash["Stash<br/>s to stash · g to apply<br/>P to pop · d to drop"]
    branches ~~~ commits ~~~ stash
  end
  subgraph global["Global controls"]
    direction LR
    navigation["Focus and movement<br/>Tab / Shift+Tab to switch panels<br/>j / k or arrow keys to move"]
    undo["Recover actions<br/>z to undo<br/>Ctrl+Z to redo"]
    session["Session controls<br/>R to refresh<br/>q to quit"]
    navigation ~~~ undo ~~~ session
  end
  working ~~~ history ~~~ global
